PILOT (not for push). _require_verbatim now reads the numbers a quote states BEFORE punctuation is removed (retrieval_log.read_numbers: decimal marks, grouping, ratios 1:12 / 1/12 / 1 in 12 / 12分の1) and requires each number of claimed_value to equal one as a number. Before: 12 under '1.2 m', 0.6 under '6.0 s', 1:1 and 112 under '1:12' and 'twelve' were ACCEPTED. After: refused; 1.2 vs '1,2 m', 1200 vs '1 200 mm' and 1:12 vs 十二分の一 still accepted. A numerical/range claimed_value with no number is refused; an ambiguous 1.200 is refused asking for the unambiguous form. _verbatim_norm, now unread, is deleted. Sweep: one caller (insert_extraction, reached by add-extraction and derive-extraction); no view, skill or registry hit. Census of stored rows: 2 non-exempt rows would be refused (extractions 30 and 80), listed not amended.

